<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Banking on a national brand': Bolsonaro sons Carlos, Jair Renan run for power in Brazil's south</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aac486af8f8bd5fc41b62b97223bf176fe93d0e36c5c309777027c08077411f5</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T17:46:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-bolsonaro-sons-carlos-and-race-for-power-brazil-south" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro is not the only member of his family campaigning in his father’s shadow. The former president's eldest son, who is now polling neck and neck with incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, can count on two of his brothers, who are standing in the senatorial and legislative elections. In Santa Catarina, one of Brazil’s most pro-Bolsonaro southern states, their surname alone is enough to secure victory.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico to sue Trump administration after White House ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f0b8d845c3011de1a6d7473f8b3726cb6469d9904468d5658cde5102042c74</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T14:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-cnn-ms-now-politico-sue-trump-administration-after-white-house-ban--1eae5b26a76f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-cnn-ms-now-politico-sue-trump-administration-after-white-house-ban" /><summary type="html">US media outlets CNN, MS NOW and Politico announced Monday they were filing suit after US President Donald Trump banned their journalists from the White House last week. The ban on the three outlets marks an escalation in the Trump administration's years-long assault on the country's press freedoms.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Midterm elections: Trump looms large over 2026 vote as Democrats eye gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ee8b42d04a912f2b93d69cdbb00da8a690f756caedd63f2b305ceef28b04512</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T12:51:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/midterm-elections-trump-looms-large-over-2026-vote-as-democrats-eye-gains--8893a9a014d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/midterm-elections-trump-looms-large-over-2026-vote-as-democrats-eye-gains" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections now just six weeks away, we’ll speak to our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson about whether President Donald Trump could help or hurt his party’s chances. Polls have pointed to what some are calling a “blue wave”, with Democrats potentially regaining control of the House, while the Senate race remains more uncertain. Trump has ramped up campaigning, including spending heavily on advertising and proposing $5,000 payments to voters who support Republicans. But with his approval ratings under pressure amid the war in Iran and the Middle East, and rising oil, gasoline and commodity prices compared with before he took office, the political landscape could still shift significantly in the coming weeks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Protests erupt after ICE shooting in Texas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b09ed8fced30da74fcde58d3f4c2819111d540f62793d74b8b9f3f6ce1bda60</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:03:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/protests-erupt-after-ice-shooting-in-texas--235cc568ff71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/protests-erupt-after-ice-shooting-in-texas" /><summary type="html">Protests have broken out in Austin, Texas, after a US Immigration and Customs Enforcement officer shot and wounded a man during a traffic stop. The man remains in serious but stable condition in hospital, while anti-ICE protesters quickly gathered at the scene. Austin’s police chief said local officers were not involved in the shooting. Ellen Gainsford reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Colombia battles massive wildfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44f4b011d34b3dc37d5a4da5f39a7a04c2e197bcb9a513197e84d18bf75f31d9</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T09:00:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/colombia-battles-massive-wildfire--3e4a063c1c7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/colombia-battles-massive-wildfire" /><summary type="html">Colombia’s disaster risk agency says a forest fire in the centre of the country is now partially under control. Around 250 firefighters, supported by volunteers, have been battling the blaze since Saturday, with some 200 hectares affected. Camille Corcoran takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Deportation project: 72 journalists investigate US treatment of migrants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7461370e5d8dabd5d0bec68c7043c08ed8273e220f3c298444c7d5be8cb02e4b</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T08:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-deportation-project-72-journalists-investigate-us-treatment-of-migrants-1--dea57e7ef702.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260921-deportation-project-72-journalists-investigate-us-treatment-of-migrants-1" /><summary type="html">Under secretive deals with countries across Africa and Latin America, the Trump administration has deported thousands of migrants to countries they had never previously visited. Of the 25,000 deportations documented by reporters, the vast majority were sent across the border to Mexico. One of the journalists who investigated the story, Sofía Álvarez Jurado, explains how these people are forced across the borders to Mexico and what happens to them once they arrive.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump to meet Macron in New York before UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5147918e3bee0ebb32a5077108550685f3791705af21b1eaea8407c6fa61766e</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T06:36:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-trump-to-meet-macron-in-new-york-before-un-general-assembly--0de11875e136.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-trump-to-meet-macron-in-new-york-before-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump will meet with French President Emmanuel Macron on Monday in New York, where both leaders will be attending the United Nations General Assembly this week, the White House said.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Third-country removals: Trump’s deportation policy by the numbers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8a15fad783bec4be3c470301e3c2529bc2ee643d7302bfe124077132e0bc625</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-third-country-removals-trump-deportation-policy-numbers--6d700771bc51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-third-country-removals-trump-deportation-policy-numbers" /><summary type="html">Since January 2025, the Trump administration has deported more than 25,000 people to so-called “third countries” – places that are not their countries of origin. Working with a team of 26 international media outlets, Forbidden Stories and FRANCE 24 have used information gathered by NGOs and open-source information to count and map these deportations. Our investigation shines a light on the scale of this mass deportation campaign that is being carried out under the cover of darkness.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>ICE, Trump and Africa: Secret deals, broken lives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:356d41e0c773f64cc3e8f2e204619f584206d2b8565466729142b598f34bb222</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T05:00:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260921-ice-trump-and-africa-secret-deals-broken-lives--a4dce10e3903.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260921-ice-trump-and-africa-secret-deals-broken-lives" /><summary type="html">For this edition of Reporters+, Karina Chabour investigated the dark side of US President Donald Trump’s immigration policy: How ICE deports immigrants to so-called third countries in Africa, far from the United States and often far from their countries of origin.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>US, China discuss opening an AI communication channel ahead of Trump-Xi summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d83e809e434784d0de20a148adfbddcc1b05658bc19e25e9035586252bc6be08</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T02:22:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-china-discuss-ai-safety-ahead-of-trump-xi-summit--f6aa3899454b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260921-us-china-discuss-ai-safety-ahead-of-trump-xi-summit" /><summary type="html">US and Chinese officials discussed creating a communication channel over potentially serious AI incidents during talks in New York on Sunday as the two sides sought progress on technology and trade ahead of this week’s summit between US President Donald Trump and his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>The Deportation Project: Inside the Trump administration's secret deals to expel people worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:175867e8ad5c1ebedd1e129fee8a4c9d4a1f729c4c989bb305a89c7e62720d55</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T17:08:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260920-the-deportation-project-inside-the-trump-administration-s-secret-deals-to-expel-people-worl--8f166565a178.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260920-the-deportation-project-inside-the-trump-administration-s-secret-deals-to-expel-people-worldwide" /><summary type="html">A consortium of 72 journalists from 26 media outlets coordinated by Forbidden Stories have been working on the Deportation Project for months. On Monday, we will take you inside the Trump administration's secret deals to expel people worldwide.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran calls Gaza war catastrophic after dropping Macklemore over pro-Palestinian comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cffd0b7d8f76046860e92395d5e4bbf92bda380154328c3abe2a584cecd0d7c8</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:57:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments--d2197bc47b01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-war-catastrophic-after-dropping-macklemore-over-pro-palestinian-comments" /><summary type="html">English singer Ed Sheeran opened his first show since his opener Macklemore was dropped after making pro-Palestinian comments onstage. The move sparked controversy and prompted several other support acts to drop out of the tour, publishing statements citing their support for Palestinians. While some concert goers could be seen trying to sell their tickets on Saturday, others have voiced their support for the 'Shape of You' singer. Story by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Three media outlets barred from the White House over 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ace124d067522940cf028388b72009089065b005611763a8f4fa81e554f8e7</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:55:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news--17d25c5dc65b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/three-media-outlets-barred-from-the-white-house-over-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has suggested that more news outlets may be barred from the White House after he announced he was banning Politico, CNN and MS NOW. On Saturday, all three outlets said that the White House confiscated their teams' press passes; they have also hinted at legal action. The ban has come under sharp criticism from press freedom advocates, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:101823ca1e55c09313ac5f5ed1585f6d08b7b69566de60f5e65964e6a568a3b6</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:40:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal--0d08e05eec1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal" /><summary type="html">The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentines protest Milei's austerity, demanding higher wages and public spending</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c90a4b15e0f596599595f2baf839947ea0e6c8611b287bd3aaf5081e348aecd</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending--b313c3b28766.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/argentines-protest-milei-s-austerity-demanding-higher-wages-and-public-spending" /><summary type="html">Tensions are boiling over in Argentina, where a massive wave of public anger is spilling onto the streets of the capital. Following months of aggressive economic reforms and rising household debt, hundreds took to the streets in a "March of Anger", targeting President Javier Milei's austerity agenda. Details by Caitlin Brown.</summary></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico reporters blocked from White House after Trump ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e2029430f299fa8a39b5398f8e36a4bed97dafc4e25a314cc27a824e7cda072</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:02:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban--a8c3f3f48609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cnn-ms-now-politico-reporters-blocked-from-white-house-after-trump-ban" /><summary type="html">White House correspondents for CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Saturday were blocked from entering the US president's office and residence a day after President Donald Trump announced he was banning the three media outlets for what he called "fake news" coverage. News organisations and press freedom groups have slammed the move as unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Millions without power in Cuba as electrical grid collapses again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a24192c871fcf581f0b7f668124fa62fc3767d0766abd5f2c874eeba25e6c71</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:01:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again--8d09cc02680d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/millions-without-power-in-cuba-as-electrical-grid-collapses-again" /><summary type="html">Cuba was plunged into its seventh massive blackout of the year on Friday. The island of over nine million people endures constant power cuts due to the poor state of its aging thermoelectric plants – but the situation has worsened significantly since January, when Washington imposed a de facto energy blockade on the island. Story by Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump claims son repaid Russian oligarch who funded wedding festivities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8553cb790021f93dd7a97ab574975993c6fb31f72d5beee5fc25969692e7bcd0</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities--ec19dbba0a0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-trump-says-son-repaid-russian-oligarch-who-funded-wedding-festivities" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Friday that his eldest son had repaid a Kremlin-linked Russian businessman who funded two days of lavish wedding celebrations in the Bahamas, after the gift raised questions over foreign influence and ethics.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump bans three media outlets from the White House, accusing them of spreading 'fake news'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c0d639bf0aa298d3b056d0580c3939edf673cc9078d5108c1f85032bb37ef8e</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:53:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news--728977f11446.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-bans-three-media-outlets-from-the-white-house-accusing-them-of-spreading-fake-news" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump announced Friday he is banning CNN, MS NOW and Politico from the White House, accusing all three outlets of spreading 'fake news'. The move is almost certain to face legal challenges, and has been denounced by press freedom advocates. The US president's relationship with media outlets has long been fraught, as Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scientists discover first new wild cat in more than 100 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c8ee764e7173100762afa23e91d1a5cf350e22c57ab782e589631e5ffb66bf7</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:44:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years--a1fa381b5177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-scientists-discover-first-new-wild-cat-in-more-than-100-years" /><summary type="html">Scientists have identified a previously unknown species of wild cat living at a wildlife sanctuary in Bolivia. The tiny, spotted feline had lived at the sanctuary for years before genetic analysis revealed it as the first new living wild cat species identified in more than a century.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Cuba hit with another nationwide blackout amid US fuel blockade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2457940d6f32ca4ce73ca7f9f5a995c45dd404d6d92600531fa0a09c007a7e1b</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:31:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness--27a189638edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-cuba-s-power-grid-collapses-again-leaving-island-in-darkness" /><summary type="html">Cuba suffered a total blackout after the collapse of its electrical grid on Friday. The blackout is the latest of at least six partial or total grid collapses since the beginning of this year, as the island grapples with an ongoing US fuel blockade.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Pop star Ed Sheeran calls situation in Gaza 'unjustifiable' amid controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7872e74ddd941cfc4d16c3c371456cf763eb0ad1b172d693d319d946ab2d064b</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T05:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-situation-unjustifiable-amid-controversy--0909b0ea7b72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260919-ed-sheeran-calls-gaza-situation-unjustifiable-amid-controversy" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran called the situation in Gaza “catastrophic and unjustifiable” on Saturday, speaking out for the first time since a controversy erupted over his tour’s removal of US rapper Macklemore after he made pro-Palestinian comments.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump bans media outlets CNN, MSNOW and Politico from the White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f4bcf5fe1ac4af1032030ddc916d58a574832813e91a2f75c6bbf7ff268305d</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:20:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-trump-bans-media-outlets-cnn-msnow-and-politico-from-white-house--abb8bd60e309.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-trump-bans-media-outlets-cnn-msnow-and-politico-from-white-house" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Friday said he would ban media outlets CNN, MSNOW and Politico from the White House over what he described as unfavourable coverage in his latest test of the US Constitution's First Amendment protection of press freedom.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>War in Iran 'jeopardises the Trump presidency', ex-Obama National Security Council member says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce98a48d677b97e2b6b0c9edceba8310d7488663daef6e38af874ed8de4406e8</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T17:01:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260918-war-in-iran-jeopardises-the-trump-presidency-ex-obama-national-security-council-member-says--08a330c92643.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260918-war-in-iran-jeopardises-the-trump-presidency-ex-obama-national-security-council-member-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, former Obama administration National Security Council member Charles Kupchan said the war in Iran "in many respects jeopardises the Trump presidency", calling it "yet another failed war of choice" that has driven up fuel and living costs ahead of the midterms. Trump's advisers "prize loyalty over fact", he added.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>A Sydney Sweeney ad goes viral: Are we all just being played?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcf2e93ff845f8ccbc26e8850026af69909eacc90598479071267e37d2d46762</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T16:27:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260918-sydney-sweeney-ad-goes-viral-are-we-all-just-being-played--40a2b8d26263.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260918-sydney-sweeney-ad-goes-viral-are-we-all-just-being-played" /><summary type="html">Another Sydney Sweeney ad goes viral – this time promoting a sports betting application almost naked. The campaign sparked fury among female athletes who said it undermines decades of progress in women's sports. Yet is the outrage itself part of the overall marketing strategy and ‘feminist-baiting’ merely a tool to get clicks?</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Fear and broken families: Inside a Texas ICE detention centre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1aa70ba3a3756be52e4ab9ea7de78ccc7e9dbe467ce60bec6dfce5ec54778f45</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260918-reporters-fear-and-broken-families-inside-a-texas-ice-detention-centre--548ff42e0c58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260918-reporters-fear-and-broken-families-inside-a-texas-ice-detention-centre" /><summary type="html">Since Donald Trump’s return to the White House in January 2025, migrant arrests have surged in the United States. More than 610,000 people have passed through detention centres run by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), the federal immigration agency in under two years. The pace only continues to accelerate: in August 2026, nearly 51,000 arrests were made in a single month – a record for Trump’s second term. Who are the people being held in these centres? What are their living conditions like? And how is Trump’s mass deportation policy upending the lives of families settled in the United States? In this report, Valérie Defert and Pierrick Leurent investigate the issue in Texas – the heart of the new US immigration detention system.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Early voting begins in US midterms that could see Republicans lose control of Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f51028d46b120891ea13abbacb0a59b51abbc475e96c358fd931a4aa24816046</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-early-voting-begins-in-us-midterms-that-could-see-republicans-lose-control-of-congress--90b2796051a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-early-voting-begins-in-us-midterms-that-could-see-republicans-lose-control-of-congress" /><summary type="html">In-person early voting for the US midterm elections begins Friday, six weeks ahead of the final November 3 vote, which will determine whether Republicans will maintain their majority in the US House and Senate. Some of the main issues American voters are deciding on are how to navigate the cost-of-living crisis, the war in Iran and President Donald Trump’s aggressive immigration enforcement campaign.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rare Aztec manuscript returns to Mexico on loan after nearly two centuries in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:865528a432b3aea9d8ce64330f5c770bdc80e6e9f11664a6854a671ea86a6443</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T22:56:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-rare-aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-on-loan-after-nearly-two-centuries-in-france--48ae560de03b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260917-rare-aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-on-loan-after-nearly-two-centuries-in-france" /><summary type="html">A prized 16th-century manuscript chronicling the rise and fall of the Aztec Empire has gone on display in Mexico City, nearly two centuries after it was taken to France, as Mexico continues to press Paris for its permanent return.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Russian disinformation campaign targets Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de885cabbf6e81050dfaa14eabca7f94273324008892db81d73ca0b1262d8864</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T21:19:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260917-us-midterms-russian-disinformation-campaign-targets-democrats--cfb73bd53905.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260917-us-midterms-russian-disinformation-campaign-targets-democrats" /><summary type="html">With US midterm elections now less than two months away, a series of videos have surfaced online, featuring celebrities seemingly denouncing the Democrats. However, the clips are fake, and were created using AI, as FRANCE 24's Charlotte Hughes explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>The Canada-EU partnership 'a classic win-win situation', economist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:489ca367c6eaa0e59d138726f19a54a10f0ab5b9ef5ee6cc36da7e43fa775d5d</id><updated>2026-09-21T20:28:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T21:12:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260917-the-canada-eu-partnership-a-classic-win-win-situation-economist-says--9faf9f8ad86c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260917-the-canada-eu-partnership-a-classic-win-win-situation-economist-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Fabian Zuleeg, Chief Economist at the European Policy Center, says that the partnership between Canada and the EU "is a classic win-win situation – Canada has many resources, has many of the economic strengths that the European Union lacks, the EU has a very large market, it is an important trading partner".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry></feed>
